Third-party software
--------------------

THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES        the Rust crates built into popcornstash and boringtun-cli,
                            with their license texts
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES-web    the npm packages bundled into the web app, with their
                            license texts (also served at /third-party-licenses.txt)

The Docker image is based on Debian. /usr/share/doc/popcornstash/debian-packages.txt
lists every Debian package in it with its version; the license of each is in
/usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright, and its source code, including that of the GPL
builds of ffmpeg, x264 and x265, is at
https://snapshot.debian.org/package/<source package>/<source version>/.

boringtun-cli is built from the boringtun and boringtun-cli crates published by
Cloudflare, with a small patch (see the Dockerfile) that lets it run on hosts
without IPv6. The vendored librqbit crates carry patches described in
vendor/*/PATCHED.md.
